    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="35ac4284-8761-5182-a9f1-edca6a198dd4" activityNameId="c8cdb029-f2ea-5b3d-8fd6-119b99308fe7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Potato starch, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Potato starch, at plant
The potatoes used as input refer to IP production. In the reference the inventory is based on, by-products evolving during starch production were allocated on an economic basis. The inventory refers to potato starch with a water content of 20% by weight.;
UUID: 4cabab9c-da5b-32e6-b114-02a06c1deccb
The production steps required to obtain potato starch from potato tubers were taken into account, including washing of the potatoes, chopping, separation of the potato fruit water, washing, refinering and finally drying of the starch. Processing of process water was included. Infrastructure use is consideration.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Refers to typical potato starch production in Germany.
Time period: Year when the data for this inventory was delivered.
Production volume: 600'000 tons in Germany (1998)
Sampling: Data based on a detailed literature study. 
Extrapolations: Potato production in Germany approximated by Swiss data.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4cabab9c-da5b-32e6-b114-02a06c1deccb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
